Ladybird’s getUniform() finds the type of the uniform at a location by
asking for the location of each element of each active uniform, then
returns the value as that type dictates. From their source, Blink’s
WebGLRenderingContextBase::getUniform() finds the type the same way, and
WebKit’s matches the location against the program’s activeUniforms().
Run, the test’s output matches Chrome 158, Firefox 151 (which returns
the values from ClientWebGLContext::GetUniform()), and WebKit 26.5, line
for line: An array uniform’s location gives its first element, and a
bool vector comes back as an Array of booleans.
